5. Use ChatGPT to explain the difference between SELinux and AppArmor in one paragraph, then write a summary in your own words and mention one real-world app (like Zomato or Paytm) that would benefit from these security modules.
==>SELinux (Security-Enhanced Linux) is a mandatory access control (MAC) system originally from the NSA that labels every process, file, and resource with a security context and enforces fine-grained policies based on those labels (Type Enforcement, Role-Based Access Control, Multi-Level Security). AppArmor is also a MAC system but uses path-based profiles: it confines individual applications by explicitly allowing or denying access to specific file paths, capabilities, and network resources. SELinux is generally considered more powerful and complex (policy is label-oriented and system-wide); AppArmor is simpler to understand and manage because policies are written against file paths rather than abstract labels.
